UID:event_317480661@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064930Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T173000
SUMMARY:Chester County Horse-Shoe and More Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike in rural Chester County Pennsylvania\
 , featuring some prominent trails including the Horse-Shoe Trail\, as well
  as other connections!\nI have planned this one specifically because it is
  a Sunday that hunting isn't permitted in some of the preserves along the 
 way\, and because most of the route is pleasant but within safety zones.\n
 After meeting at Bryn Coed\, we will shuttle with as few vehicles as possi
 ble to our start point\, at Highland Farm Park.\nWe'll start by walking so
 me of the trails to the north\, through fields and a wood line\, out into 
 a development.\nWe'll cut through the development and then out to the Pick
 ering Creek Trail.\nWe'll take the Station Blvd Trail north to the Eagle F
 arms Trail east\, then turn onto the pleasant Chester Springs Road.\nThe l
 ightly trafficked road will lead us to the Horse-Shoe Trail where we last 
 left off on it.\nWe'll follow Horse-Shoe Trail east for a bit\, and then t
 urn off at Bodine Road.\nWe'll follow a short road bit to the Hickory Trai
 l which takes us north more.\nFrom the Elbow Road\, we'll reach the Binky 
 Lee Preserve and pass through fields and woods. We'll exit the north side 
 from that\, and then follow some more back roads for a bit.\nLightly used 
 Kimberton Road and Flint Road will take us to Bryn Coed Preserve for the l
 ast leg of the hike.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374\nDistance wil
 l be about 15 miles.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/317480661/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261118T121956Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T121956Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_317480209@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064930Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T193000
SUMMARY:Holiday New York City Hike!
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for our annual Holiday New York City Hike!\nThis year\, we'll meet
  at New York Penn Station\, in the mall type area with the large Christmas
  tree like we usually do (it's in the cover photo here).\nThis would be th
 e big circular area in NY Penn Station.\nFrom there\, we'll all take the s
 ubway north to Van Cortland Park\, Bronx\, and we'll start with a bunch of
  the trails there we've never done before.\nFrom there\, we head west towa
 rd the Hudson River where we'll begin heading south on some of the trails 
 and walkways.\nWe'll walk the newly reopened pedestrian lanes over Henry H
 udson Bridge and then follow slopes though Inwood Hills Park and Fort Tryo
 n Park.\nAfter this\, we'll try to take the Hudson River Greenway and Empi
 re State Trail\, but keep to the more middle section of it. We've done the
  upper and lower bits in the past\, so this is an opportunity to do some o
 f the other middle ground.\nWe're planning on doing about fifteen miles\, 
 but in the city\, people can cut out just about any time with all of the p
 ublic transportation.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374\nNOTE that w
 hen you arrive\, use the restroom right away. Every year\, we end up waiti
 ng around\, and then after waiting around and we're about ready to go\, ev
 eryone decides they want to use the restroom. Don't do that!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/317480209/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261118T113258Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T113258Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
